the fast festival culminates on May 7th  with fast light which will be an event  that illuminates all of mi t--'s campus  and waterfront there are series of  installations by the faculty in the  department of architecture there will  also be a series of pavilions that are  open to the public they are doing a kind  of range of projects from photovoltaic  soft rockers which multiple people can  sit on and absorb energy and light up in  the evenings two collaborations between  architects and performance artists or  architects and video artists where the  design of the pavilion is specific to  the work of art being featured in the  pavilion several art installations will  be in the river and work off the  reflection of the water etc at nighttime  these installations will be interactive  so they'll invite the public into them  to actually contribute to the  choreography of the light we also wanted  to involve the amazing MIT students and  so we had an open competition this was  open to schools across campus we had  proposals that were all incredibly  fascinating to the point where we didn't  know actually if the proposal came from  an artist and architect a biologist or a  physics major one student project is  called the ice wall which consists of  these kind of large ice cubes built that  will build a kind of wall and embedded  in these cubes are seeds that when they  melt they'll you know become flowerbeds  in the spring and then there's a time  capsule video piece by another student  from the Media Lab and then there are  larger environmentally scaled  installations by students like a string  tunnel on campus that will just take a  kind of mundane everyday space at MIT  and for a couple of weeks transform it  into  a special environment the amazing thing  about the MIT students is that they are  completely fearless they have no  boundaries their interdisciplinary by  nature they benefit so much from MIT as  an institute by being able to take  classes across all of the schools and I  think this really is reflected in the  projects that they are going to be doing  for the fast festival in that they are  incredibly creative and innovative and  they have a certain quality of magic and  optimism about technology the arts and  the future  you
 

